{
  "info": {
    "name": "Pedidos360 - Matriz de seguridad EP1",
    "description": "Colección lista para ejecutar con el Collection Runner durante la defensa.\n\nANTES DE CORRER:\n1. Importa también Pedidos360.postman_environment.json y selecciónalo arriba a la derecha.\n2. Obtén los dos tokens con: pruebas\\obtener-token.ps1 -Cuenta Cliente@... (y luego Admin@...)\n3. Pega cada uno en las variables tokenCliente y tokenAdmin del environment.\n\nLas carpetas están ordenadas para ejecutarse de arriba hacia abajo: la primera captura los ids que usan las siguientes.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "productoId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "pedidoId", "value": "" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Preparación",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Leer catálogo desde Oracle",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const productos = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Hay productos cargados en Oracle', () => pm.expect(productos.length).to.be.above(0));",
                  "const disponible = productos.find(p => p.activo && p.stock > 5) || productos[0];",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('productoId', disponible.id);",
                  "console.log('Producto elegido:', disponible.sku, '| stock actual:', disponible.stock);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{tokenCliente}}" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/catalog", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "catalog"] },
            "description": "Recorre toda la cadena: API Gateway → BFF → ms-catalog → Oracle."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Crear pedido de prueba (Admin)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const pedido = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('pedidoId', pedido.id);",
                  "pm.test('Nace en estado CREADO', () => pm.expect(pedido.estado).to.eql('CREADO'));",
                  "console.log('Pedido creado:', pedido.codigo);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}" },
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"clienteEmail\": \"Admin@luissantacruz2026.onmicrosoft.com\",\n  \"clienteNombre\": \"Demostracion EP1\",\n  \"direccionEntrega\": \"Duoc UC\",\n  \"items\": [\n    { \"productoId\": {{productoId}}, \"cantidad\": 1 }\n  ]\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/orders", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "orders"] }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1. Matriz de seguridad (pauta §6)",
      "description": "Los cinco escenarios que exige la pauta, más el preflight CORS.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Sin token → 401 (rechaza API Gateway)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('401 Unauthorized', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));",
                  "pm.test('El rechazo viene del Gateway, no del BFF', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.include('Unauthorized');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/orders", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "orders"] },
            "description": "El JWT Authorizer rechaza en el borde. La petición nunca llega al BFF."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Token inválido → 401",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": ["pm.test('401 Unauthorized', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJmYWxzbyJ9.firma_que_no_corresponde" }
            ],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/orders", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "orders"] },
            "description": "Firma que no corresponde a las claves públicas de Entra ID."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Acceso permitido (Cliente) → 200",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Devuelve datos reales desde Oracle', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.be.an('array');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{tokenCliente}}" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/orders", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "orders"] },
            "description": "Atraviesa las cinco capas: Gateway → BFF → ms-orders → Oracle."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Rol sin permiso (Cliente en /accept) → 403",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('403 Forbidden', () => pm.response.to.have.status(403));",
                  "pm.test('No es 401: el token es válido, falla la autorización', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.not.eql(401);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{tokenCliente}}" }],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{pedidoId}}/accept",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "orders", "{{pedidoId}}", "accept"]
            },
            "description": "El Gateway deja pasar el token porque es válido. Quien rechaza es el BFF, con @PreAuthorize sobre el claim roles."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Regla de negocio (/ship sin aceptar) → 400",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('400 Bad Request', () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "pm.test('El microservicio explica el motivo', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().mensaje).to.include('no puede pasar');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('Indica las transiciones válidas', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().detalles[0]).to.include('ACEPTADO');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}" }],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{pedidoId}}/ship",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "orders", "{{pedidoId}}", "ship"]
            },
            "description": "La máquina de estados del microservicio impide despachar sin aceptar. Rol correcto, operación inválida."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Preflight CORS sin token → 200",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('No exige token', () => pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 204]));",
                  "pm.test('Devuelve Access-Control-Allow-Origin', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Access-Control-Allow-Origin')).to.not.be.null;",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "OPTIONS",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Origin", "value": "http://localhost:4200" },
              { "key": "Access-Control-Request-Method", "value": "GET" },
              { "key": "Access-Control-Request-Headers", "value": "authorization" }
            ],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/orders", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "orders"] },
            "description": "El navegador no envía Authorization en el preflight. Si esta ruta llevara authorizer, CORS se rompería con un 401."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Máquina de estados (Admin)",
      "description": "Recorrido completo. Cada transición descuenta o valida según corresponda.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "accept → ACEPTADO (descuenta stock)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Estado ACEPTADO', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().estado).to.eql('ACEPTADO'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}" }],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{pedidoId}}/accept",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "orders", "{{pedidoId}}", "accept"]
            },
            "description": "Única transición que llama al microservicio de catálogo para descontar stock."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "prepare → EN_PREPARACION",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Estado EN_PREPARACION', () => {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().estado).to.eql('EN_PREPARACION');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}" }],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{pedidoId}}/prepare",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "orders", "{{pedidoId}}", "prepare"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "ship → DESPACHADO",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Estado DESPACHADO', () => {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().estado).to.eql('DESPACHADO');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}" }],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{pedidoId}}/ship",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "orders", "{{pedidoId}}", "ship"]
            },
            "description": "Ahora sí funciona: el pedido está en EN_PREPARACION. Es la misma petición que antes daba 400."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "deliver → ENTREGADO",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Estado ENTREGADO', () => {",
                  "    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().estado).to.eql('ENTREGADO');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('ENTREGADO es estado final', () => {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.json().transicionesPermitidas).to.be.an('array').that.is.empty;",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}" }],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{pedidoId}}/deliver",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "orders", "{{pedidoId}}", "deliver"]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Verificar stock descontado",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const p = pm.response.json().find(x => x.id === Number(pm.collectionVariables.get('productoId')));",
                  "console.log('Stock final de', p.sku, ':', p.stock);",
                  "pm.test('El producto sigue existiendo en Oracle', () => pm.expect(p).to.not.be.undefined);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [{ "key": "Authorization", "value": "Bearer {{tokenAdmin}}" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/catalog", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["api", "catalog"] },
            "description": "Compara el stock con el que imprimió la consola en el primer paso: bajó por la llamada entre microservicios."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
